<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στομόω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>muzzle</i> or
			<i>gag</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.69
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώλους . . φιμοῖσιν . .
				ἐστομωμένας</span>
			<i>having their mouths muzzled</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				326
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>furnish with a mouth</i> or <i>opening</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					2.100
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Medic.,=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναστομόω</span>, <i>open</i>,
			either by the knife, or by plasters, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				40
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.8.21
			</span></i>; <i>dilate</i>, of the womb, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>provide with a mouth</i>, i.e. with eloquence, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cret.</u>
				44
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111.1
				</span></i>
			) of iron, <i>harden, make into steel</i>, in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				102.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.943e
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχος] ἐστομωμένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					790.5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Achaea</span>); Chrysippus compared the
			creation of the soul to the <i>hardening</i> of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεῦμα</span> in the cold air, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.134
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				222
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>steel, harden, train</i> for anything, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1108
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1110
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. στομάχους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Muson.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			A<i><span class="en">
				p.97H.
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			):—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στομοῦσθαι καὶ κρατύνεσθαι [τὰ
				βρέφη</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκοντισταῖς τὴν οὐραγίαν καὶ τὰς
				πλευρὰς ς</span>. <i>edge, fringe, fence</i> with
			javelin-men, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				42
			</span></i>; so perh., in 
				Pass.
			, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράκαινα] ἐχίδναις ἐστομωμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					287
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
